  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday Night through Wednesday)\nIssued at 930 PM CST Wed Nov 18 2026\n\nSunday, a shortwave will swing through the Lower MS Valley and \nbring an increase in cloud cover and a low chance (20-30%) of \nshowers to the TN Valley. Highs will be around 70 degrees. A \ncoastal low in the Mid Atlantic will slide up along the coast \nwhile an upper level trough reaches the Upper Great Lakes. The \nassociated sfc low (Great Lakes) will have a trailing cold front \nthat will reach the forecast area on Monday. Right now, it looks \nlike the precip with it should remain to our north, but cannot \nrule out some light showers with the bkn/ovc skies. Once the front\npasses, cloud cover will start to break up and despite the \nincrease in sunshine, the CAA will win out and highs on Monday \nwill only reach the upper 50s to lower 60s. That's ~10 degrees \ncooler than Sunday. The lows Monday night will also be ~10 degrees\ncooler, falling into the 30s. As a secondary sfc low develops \nalong the tail end of the cold front to our south, it sets up an \ninverted trough over the TN Valley Tuesday and Wednesday. Here we \ncould see another low chance (15-30%) of showers return. Tuesday \ntemps will be fairly similar to Monday, however on Wednesday, the \nhighs may not get out of the 50s. If you have friends and family \ncoming into town for Thanksgiving, make sure they are also \nprepared for the colder temps!",
